    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d27-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d27-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 64 D 559, CF 1584. Secret.
                    Drafted by Pfeiffer; cleared with G, W/MSC, C, L, H, S/P, and with Ambassador
                    MacArthur and Assistant Secretary of Defense Sprague.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f2" n="1" xml:id="d27-f2-content">
                <p>Department Circular No. 175, December 13, 1955, outlined procedures for the
                    exercise of the treaty-making and executive agreement-making process of the
                    United States. (Department of State Library)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f3" n="2" xml:id="d27-f3-content">
                <p>No attachments were found with this memorandum. Tabs A and B were attached to
                    another copy of this memorandum. Tab C, Peace Treaty with Japan, September 8,
                    1951, is in 3 UST (pt. 3) 3169.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f4" n="3" xml:id="d27-f4-content">
                <p>Approved by Dulles on September 29.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
